menu "MiezMerker board"
config MM_DEV_SYNTHETIC_INPUT
    bool "Enable bounded synthetic RFID commands on the USB console"
    default n
    help
        Development only. Commands use the real Core capture and NVS path.
        Does not weaken authorization or expose a BLE injection endpoint.
config MM_DEV_GPIO_RFID
    bool "Enable development GPIO pushbutton RFID reader"
    default n
    help
        Explicit development build only. Active LOW with internal pull-up.
        Each debounced press offers one random demo chip 1..5 to the real Core.
        Requires CMake MM_DEVELOPMENT_BUILD=ON; release builds reject this flag.
config MM_DEV_GPIO_RFID_PIN
    int "Development RFID button GPIO"
    depends on MM_DEV_GPIO_RFID
    range 0 10
    default 3
    help
        SuperMini GPIO3 is unused. GPIO2/8/9 are forbidden strapping/BOOT pins.
        USB18/19 and flash pins are outside this range. Recheck wiring conflicts
        before selecting another pin or adding real reader/RTC hardware.
config MM_ISSUER_PUBLIC_KEY_HEX
    string "Independently pinned backend P-256 public key (130 hex characters)"
    default ""
    help
        Uncompressed 04 || x || y, obtained from the trusted deployment.
        Empty means fail closed for credentials and receipts. No private issuer key.
endmenu
